    "reconstruction_notes": {
      "en": "Original living whole-organism interpretation: elongated flattened soft mantle and sole, one cap shell near each end, ordered overlapping dorsal armour and short marginal sclerites. Simplified counts and muted green-grey shell colors are artistic choices, not measured fossil evidence. Molluscan-inspired classification is retained; no reptile identity, exact phylogenetic conclusion, mouthparts, locomotor mechanism or microstructure claimed. Closed armour roots intentionally overlap the continuous mantle.",
      "zh": "原创全身生活复原：长扁软体背部与腹足、前后两端各一枚帽壳、有序叠片背甲和短边缘骨片。简化数量及柔和灰绿色配色为美术设定，非化石测量。保留软体动物启发分类，不当作爬行类，不主张精确系统位置、口器、运动机制或微观结构。封闭骨片根部有意嵌入连续外套体。"
    },
    "reconstruction_type": "whole-organism",
